{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112256","id":2967753118,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6w5FGe","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112256","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112256.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112256.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112256","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112256/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112256/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112256/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/375c6d0337dc2b283d8f3a3575781bd9144d5e08","number":112256,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix discrepancy in int handling between JSON::stringify and JSON::parse_string","user":{"login":"Chkoupinator","id":7254970,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTQ5NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7254970?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator","html_url":"https://github.com/Chkoupinator","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I am proposing a fix for the issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/24119 which I had the displeasure of running through myself following the behavior mentioned by https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8830 in the hopes of helping bring an end to this (7 years old!!! debate)\r\n\r\nCurrently, Godot claims to follow the official JSON spec, stating in the documentation of stringify: \"[...] converting a Variant to JSON text will convert all numerical values to float types\". [source](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_json.html#class-json-method-stringify).\r\n\r\nHowever, this is factually not true as can be seen in the code of stringify, when an INTEGER variant is detected it uses itos [(line 75 of json.cpp)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/io/json.cpp#L74), which has the very strange behavior of not loosing any precision when going \"out\" of Godot, making it look supported but then loosing precision when imported as can be seen in the modified code.\r\n\r\nThe changes in this PR hope to bring a satisfying solution to this problem by considering values that do not contain a comma or an exponent notation as an integer and storing them as such when parsing JSON.\r\n\r\nThis would make Godot follow the [OpenAPI spec](https://spec.openapis.org/registry/format/int64) for JSON instead of the official spec which does not support integers.\r\n\r\n### What does it break?\r\nAny reliance on Variant types generated by the JSON parser not including INTEGER would break\r\n\r\n### What does it fix?\r\nUsers naïvely expecting to be able to stringify then parse an int64 or a PackedInt64Array would not be surprised to see that the value of their integers have changed when importing.\r\n\r\nFrom what I have understood storing uids in a JSON is the preferred way when referencing Resources in a save system so this is in my opinion critical.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5796,"closed_issues":0,"created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T09:35:07Z","closed_at":null,"due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-10-31T18:44:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T20:10:03Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":